        "original_id": "0f152b6f-212d-59d2-b750-7d1dab5e29e1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 1993 Liberty Bowl\n- Organizations: Big Ten Conference\n- Teams: Michigan State Spartans\n- Places: Liberty Bowl Memorial Stadium, Memphis, Tennessee\n- Topics: 1993–94 bowl season\n\nFacts:\n- The 1993 Liberty Bowl was a college football bowl game played on December 28, 1993 at Liberty Bowl Memorial Stadium in Memphis, Tennessee.\n- The 1993 Liberty Bowl was part of the 1993–94 bowl season.\n- The Michigan State Spartans of the Big Ten Conference accepted an invitation to the 1993 Liberty Bowl.\n- The Big Ten Conference, also called the B1G and formerly known as the Western Conference and Big Nine Conference, is the oldest Division I collegiate athletic conference in the United States.\n- As of 2016, the Big Ten Conference had 14 members despite its name.",
